# SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0
# Mustfile — Physical state contract for my-lang
# Author: Jonathan D.A. Jewell <j.d.a.jewell@open.ac.uk>
#
# What MUST be true about this repository. Hard requirements.
# Run with: must check
# Fix with: must fix (where a deterministic fix exists)

@abstract:
Physical-state invariants for my-lang (the QTT multi-dialect language with a
mechanised Coq + Idris2 solo-core). These are hard requirements — CI and
pre-commit hooks fail if any check fails. my-lang is a CONSUMER of the RSR
(Rhodium Standard Repository) template, not the template itself.
@end

## File Presence

### license-present
- description: LICENSE file must exist
- run: test -f LICENSE
- severity: critical

### readme-present
- description: README.adoc must exist
- run: test -f README.adoc
- severity: critical

### security-policy
- description: SECURITY.md must exist
- run: test -f SECURITY.md
- severity: critical

### ai-manifest
- description: 0-AI-MANIFEST.a2ml must exist (under 6a2/)
- run: test -f .machine_readable/6a2/0-AI-MANIFEST.a2ml
- severity: critical

### governance-docs
- description: GOVERNANCE.adoc, MAINTAINERS.adoc, CODEOWNERS must exist
- run: test -f GOVERNANCE.adoc && test -f MAINTAINERS.adoc && test -f .github/CODEOWNERS
- severity: critical

### machine-readable-dir
- description: .machine_readable/ directory must exist
- run: test -d .machine_readable
- severity: critical

## Directory Structure

### contractiles-complete
- description: The contractiles dir exists, with bust/ and dust/ as DIRECTORIES.
    bust and dust are multi-file by design (one bust per failure-mode/issue;
    one dust per cleanup intention, e.g. uninstall / detach-component-as-plugin),
    so they are directories, not single flat files.
- run: test -d .machine_readable/contractiles && test -d .machine_readable/contractiles/bust && test -d .machine_readable/contractiles/dust
- severity: critical

### contractiles-singular-present
- description: The four SINGULAR contractile verbs exist as flat files
- run: test -f .machine_readable/contractiles/Intentfile.a2ml && test -f .machine_readable/contractiles/Mustfile.a2ml && test -f .machine_readable/contractiles/Trustfile.a2ml && test -f .machine_readable/contractiles/Adjustfile.a2ml
- severity: critical

### bust-dust-files-present
- description: bust/ and dust/ each hold at least one contractile file (more allowed)
- run: test -n "$(ls .machine_readable/contractiles/bust/*.a2ml 2>/dev/null)" && test -n "$(ls .machine_readable/contractiles/dust/*.a2ml 2>/dev/null)"
- severity: critical

### six-directory-present
- description: 6a2 directory exists with required files
- run: test -d .machine_readable/6a2 && test -f .machine_readable/6a2/META.a2ml && test -f .machine_readable/6a2/ECOSYSTEM.a2ml && test -f .machine_readable/6a2/STATE.a2ml && test -f .machine_readable/6a2/PLAYBOOK.a2ml && test -f .machine_readable/6a2/AGENTIC.a2ml && test -f .machine_readable/6a2/NEUROSYM.a2ml
- severity: critical

### scope-arrest-anchor
- description: The scope-arrest ANCHOR exists at the repo root
- run: test -n "$(ls ANCHOR.scope-arrest.*.scm 2>/dev/null)"
- severity: warning

### self-validating-structure
- description: self-validating/ exists and holds at least one k9 contract
- run: test -d .machine_readable/self-validating && test -n "$(ls .machine_readable/self-validating/*.k9.ncl 2>/dev/null)"
- severity: warning

## Identity

### identifies-as-my-lang
- description: The north-star contractile names my-lang as its subject (guards
    against re-introducing un-customised upstream-template boilerplate)
- run: grep -q 'my-lang' .machine_readable/contractiles/Intentfile.a2ml
- severity: warning
- notes: Template-identity / placeholder drift is tracked advisorily in Adjustfile.a2ml

## Git State

### no-untracked-contractiles
- description: All contractile files are tracked in git
- run: test -z "$(git ls-files -o --exclude-standard .machine_readable/contractiles/ 2>/dev/null)"
- severity: critical

### signed-commits
- description: Commits should be signed (aspirational for my-lang; not yet enforced)
- run: git verify-commit HEAD
- severity: warning
